      "value": "ooa2"
    },
    "description": {
      "value": "A polished brass metronome ticks rhythmically within the haft of this +1 striking gnome hooked hammer. Gnome adherents of Brigh often attempt to reproduce this item as part of a ritual symbolizing methodical problem-solving and thoughtful craftsmanship. By timing the sweeping arcs of your Trip attempt to the built-in metronome of a metronomic hammer, you gain a +1 item bonus to your Athletics check to Trip the target. This item bonus increases by 1 with every subsequent Trip attempt you make with the metronomic hammer against the same target this turn, to a maximum of +3 on your third Trip. The bonus resets to +1 if you successfully Trip the target, if you critically fail to Trip the target, or if your turn ends."
    },
